# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for nim-brokers.
#
# Format (one rule per line):
#   race:<substring of function/symbol>
#   deadlock:<substring>
#   called_from_lib:<shared-lib name>
#   thread:<substring>
#
# Wired in by setSanitizerEnv("tsan") via TSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=.
# Keep this list MINIMAL — only add an entry once you have confirmed the
# reported race is benign (e.g. a known-safe pattern in the Nim runtime or
# chronos internals), never to silence a real race in broker code.
#
# Nim refc/orc collector bookkeeping and chronos event-loop internals can
# produce benign reports under partial instrumentation. Add specific frames
# here as they are triaged. Example (commented out until confirmed):
# race:nimGCvisit
# race:chronos


# Nim stdlib (lib/system/threadimpl.nim, nimThreadProcWrapperBody): on exit a
# thread writes `thrd.core = nil` / `thrd.dataFn = nil` into the caller-owned
# Thread object, while `joinThread` takes that Thread BY VALUE, so the caller
# copies the whole struct before pthread_join establishes happens-before.
# The copied core/dataFn are never read (only `sys`, written before the thread
# starts). Benign, upstream. `race_top` (top frame only) keeps this narrow:
# threadProcWrapper is the bottom frame of every worker stack, so a plain
# `race:` entry would hide every worker-thread race. Seen on Linux (clang 19).
race_top:threadProcWrapper
